findings.body:
Before this PR, a failed conversation-variable write raised inside the assigner's `_run()`. The node therefore returned FAILED, and the workflow surfaced the error. Now the write happens in `ConversationVariablePersistenceLayer.on_event`, after the node has already emitted `NodeRunSucceededEvent`.

Two things make this a silent failure. First, `EventManager._notify_layers` wraps every `layer.on_event` call in `try/except Exception` and only logs it, so `ConversationVariableNotFoundError` or any SQLAlchemy error just becomes a log line. Second, the run continues and the variable pool holds the new value, so the user sees a successful run whose conversation state was never saved. The next turn will then read stale values from the DB.

::diff{file="api/core/app/layers/conversation_variable_persist_layer.py" lines="52-53"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The node contract now depends on a best-effort observer. Either persist synchronously in the node again, or make the layer's failure visible (for example, by setting a graph-level error or aborting via the command channel).
